    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-120626",
      "knowledge_point_id": "c71c49ee-e496-5d4e-87fa-96e28dd830ca",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Cotangent with Non-Special Angles",
      "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation  $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-\\frac{2}{3}$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\text{arctan}(-\\frac{3}{2})=-(56.309\\,9…)^{∘}≈-{56.310}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-{56.310}^{∘}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={180}^{∘}+x={180}^{∘}-{56.310}^{∘}={123.690}^{∘},\\,\\,{x}_{2}={360}^{∘}+x={360}^{∘}-{56.310}^{∘}={303.690}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n123.690\\cdot 303.690≈37\\,563\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.",
