    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-274561",
      "knowledge_point_id": "c71c49ee-e496-5d4e-87fa-96e28dd830ca",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Cotangent with Non-Special Angles",
      "problem": "Find, **in ascending order and rounded to the nearest integer**, the two solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}$  for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=2.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)=(63.434\\,9…)^{∘}≈{63.435}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${63.435}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution, rounded to the nearest integer, is ${x}_{1}={63}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$\nHence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+x={180}^{∘}+{63.435}^{∘}≈{243}^{∘},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x={63}^{∘}$ and $x={243}^{∘}.$",
